# ============================================================================
# What never enters the Docker build context.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. `.claude/worktrees/` holds TWO
# complete checkouts of this repository, each with its own `node_modules` and
# its own `.next`. Without the exclusions below, `docker build` uploads several
# gigabytes to the daemon before it runs a single instruction, and does it on
# every build because the context hash changes whenever either worktree does.
#
# The rule for adding to this file: if the production image does not read it at
# runtime and `next build` does not read it at build time, it does not belong in
# the context.
# ============================================================================

# ── Agent worktrees: two full duplicate checkouts ──────────────────────────
.claude/

# ── Dependencies and build output (reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image) ───
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

# ── Secrets. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT excluded: it documents the
#    variable names and carries no values. Every other .env holds real keys and
#    must never reach an image layer, where it would survive deletion.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Version control and CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky

# ── Tests and their artifacts. The image serves the app; it never runs them.
tests
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.playwright

# ── Database work. Migrations are applied against Supabase, never from the
#    running container.
supabase

# ── Editor, OS and tooling noise ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.eslintcache
.turbo
.vercel

# ── Documentation and planning ────────────────────────────────────────────
docs
*.md
!README.md

# ── Container files themselves: including them would invalidate the build
#    cache on every edit to the Caddyfile, which the app image never reads.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Caddyfile
